{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "TPL5010QDDCTQ1",
 "kind": "logic",
 "manufacturer": "Texas Instruments",
 "title": "TPL5010-Q1 automotive nano-power system timer with watchdog, 100 ms to 7200 s",
 "source": {
  "document": "SNAS679",
  "revision": "September 2016",
  "pages": 24
 },
 "summary": "An AEC-Q100 Grade 1 timer that draws 35 nA typical and runs from 1.8 V to 5.5 V. One resistor from DELAY/M_RST to ground, read once at power-up, picks one of 1650 intervals between 100 ms and 7200 s; at the start of each interval the WAKE output pulses high to rouse a sleeping microcontroller. The microcontroller answers on DONE; a missing answer pulls the open-drain RSTn output low, so the part doubles as a watchdog. Pulling DELAY/M_RST high gives a debounced manual reset. Packaged in a 6-pin SOT-23 (DDC).",
 "key_figures": [
