  {
   "id": "manual-reset-spst",
   "title": "Wake-up timer and watchdog with SPST manual reset (simplified application)",
   "page": 11,
   "description": "A battery feeds a power-management stage whose output is the common VDD for the timer and the microcontroller. REXT from DELAY/M_RST to ground sets the interval. WAKE and DONE each run to a microcontroller GPIO; RSTn drives the microcontroller reset and is pulled up to VDD by Rp. A push-button from VDD to DELAY/M_RST is the manual reset: while it is held, VDD/REXT flows through REXT.",
